# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build-context exclusions for images built from the repository root
# (the .NET images). Each service with its own build context has its own
# .dockerignore next to its Dockerfile.
#
# This file is load-bearing, not an optimisation. The .NET Dockerfiles restore
# in an early stage and then `COPY backend/ ./backend/` before publishing with
# --no-restore. Without the artifacts/obj exclusions below, that COPY drops the
# HOST's restore output on top of the container's, and the publish fails with
#
#   error NETSDK1064: Package Asp.Versioning.Abstractions, version 10.2.1 was
#   not found. It might have been deleted since NuGet restore.
#
# because the host's project.assets.json points at packages that only exist in
# the host's ~/.nuget/packages.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Version control and CI ---
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github

# --- Secrets: never let these into a build context or an image layer -------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
**/appsettings.Local.json
**/appsettings.*.Local.json
**/*.pem
**/*.p12
**/*.mobileprovision
secrets/

# --- .NET build and restore output (see the note above) --------------------
**/artifacts/
**/obj/
**/bin/
**/TestResults/
**/*.user

# --- Other ecosystems' build output and dependencies ----------------------
**/node_modules/
**/dist/
**/.venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.build/
**/.swiftpm/
**/DerivedData/
**/*.xcodeproj/

# --- Noise ----------------------------------------------------------------
**/.DS_Store
**/*.log
.vscode/
.idea/
